---
import ModuleWrapper, { type _ModuleWrapper, type _ModuleHeader } from "@/components/ui/modules/ModuleWrapper.astro";

export interface Props extends _ModuleWrapper {}

const props = Astro.props;

const header: _ModuleHeader = {
	...props.header,
	title: props.header?.title || "Education",
};
---

<ModuleWrapper {...{ ...props, header }}>
	<p>
		I was always told that <strong>"doing it is the best education"</strong>, and so while my formal education is limited, my real education has come from learning <strong>on the job</strong>.
		That has served me well, because it is real-world experience. The risk is delivering when I don't already know how, and whenever a project handed me something I couldn't do, I spent the time
		to learn it.
	</p>

	<div class="my-2 rounded border border-line bg-sunk p-5">
		<p>A quick overview of my <u>formal education</u>:</p>

		<ul class="ml-6 list-outside list-disc space-y-2">
			<li>Completed a 12 month traineeship as the network administrator for a high school.</li>
			<li>Attended the International Coaching Institute (ICI) via remote learning to get started in coaching.</li>
		</ul>
	</div>

	<p>
		I'm a continuous learner who likes understanding and solving problems, so spare time usually goes on a new skill or sharpening an existing one. Listing every course, tutorial and book would be
		a long and tedious list; the technical and transferable skills I've picked up along the way are what this CV is made of.
	</p>
</ModuleWrapper>
